// Facts about Roam Research's own CSS, learned from roamresearch.com's public
// stylesheet (assets/css/less-compiled/site.css) on 2026-09-20 and from the
// Blueprint stylesheet it serves (assets/css/npm/blueprint/core/lib/css/blueprint.css)
// on 2026-09-22, plus the
// conventions Live Themes relies on. Injected in the system prompt so the
// model reasons from Roam's real variables and defaults instead of guessing.
//
// The live DOM snapshot (domInspector.js) complements these static facts with
// what is true in the user's graph right now (installed themes, extensions,
// actual computed colors).

var ROAM_FACTS = "## Facts about Roam's own CSS (verified against roamresearch.com's stylesheet)\n- Base font: \"Inter\" (Roam loads Inter and Fira Code). Block text `.roam-block` has line-height 1.5em and 4px vertical padding; page title `.rm-title-display` has line-height 1.25em.\n- Native CSS variables defined by Roam on :root/html: `--primary-color` (#137CBD), `--background-color` (#E1E8ED), `--highlight-color` (#FBD065), `--inline-highlight-color` (hsl(51,98%,81%), used by `.rm-highlight`), spacing scale `--s0`=4px `--s1`=8px `--s2`=16px `--s3`=24px `--s4`=32px (`--s1` drives block spacing: 4px in Compact layout, 12px in Cozy), dark palette `--dark-bg` (#202B33) `--dark-bg-2` (#293742) `--dark-bg-3` (#354655) `--dark-bg-4` (#252A31) `--dark-left-bg` (#30404D) `--dark-ff` (#f5f8fa, dark-mode text) `--dark-hl` (rgba(138,155,168,0.15)) `--dark-icon-color` (#A7B6C2) `--dark-bg-embed` `--dark-highlight-yellow`, and `--callout-color` / `--_callout-bg` on each `.rm-callout--<type>`. You may reuse or override these variables.\n- Native settings exposed as attributes on <html>: `data-roam-color-theme` (\"Roam-Classic\" or \"Alexandretta\", the latter sets --primary-color #48AFF0 and --background-color #30404D) and `data-roam-layout-theme` (\"Compact\" or \"Cozy\").\n- Roam's own dark theme rules (about 200) are scoped under the Blueprint class `.bp3-dark` (`.bp3-dark { background: var(--dark-bg); color: var(--dark-ff) }`, `.bp3-dark .rm-page-ref--link { color: #48aff0 }`, `.bp3-dark .rm-bullet__inner { background-color: #738694 }`, \u2026). `.rm-dark-theme` is NOT a Roam class: it is the convention of the Dark Toggle extension and of Live Themes, added on <html> and <body>. So a dark theme written for `.rm-dark-theme` must restyle everything itself (Roam's .bp3-dark rules do not apply), including Blueprint popovers, menus and dialogs.\n- BLUEPRINT CONTROLS (verified against Roam's blueprint.css on 2026-09-22). Roam's buttons, selects, inputs, checkboxes, switches, tabs, menus, popovers and dialogs are Blueprint v3 components styled by a SEPARATE stylesheet (blueprint.css): light by default, dark only under `.bp3-dark`. Their default look is a white gradient over a pale background, so they stay LIGHT on a Live Themes dark background unless the theme restyles them. Selectors, light defaults, and in brackets the values Roam's own `.bp3-dark` uses (the natural dark palette to reproduce under `.rm-dark-theme`):\n  \xB7 Button `.bp3-button:not([class*=\"bp3-intent-\"])`: background-color #f5f8fa + background-image linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,.8), rgba(255,255,255,0)), box-shadow inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.2), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(16,22,26,.1), color #182026; `:hover` #ebf1f5; `:active` / `.bp3-active` #d8e1e8; `:disabled` / `.bp3-disabled` rgba(206,217,224,.5) text rgba(92,112,128,.6) [dark: #394b59 with gradient rgba(255,255,255,.05)\u21920, box-shadow 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.4), color #f5f8fa; hover #30404d; active #202b33; disabled rgba(57,75,89,.5) text rgba(167,182,194,.6)]. Icons inside buttons `.bp3-button .bp3-icon` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2]. Minimal (icon) buttons `.bp3-button.bp3-minimal`: transparent, hover rgba(167,182,194,.3), active rgba(115,134,148,.3), text #182026 [hover rgba(138,155,168,.15), active rgba(138,155,168,.3), text inherit then #f5f8fa]. Outlined `.bp3-button.bp3-outlined`: 1px border rgba(24,32,38,.2) [rgba(255,255,255,.4)]. Intent buttons `.bp3-intent-primary` #137cbd (hover #106ba3), `-success` #0f9960, `-warning` #d9822b, `-danger` #db3737, white text, identical in both modes: keep them unless the theme changes the accent.\n  \xB7 Select `.bp3-html-select select, .bp3-select select`: same look as a button (#f5f8fa + gradient, inset shadow, color #182026, hover #ebf1f5, active #d8e1e8) [#394b59 + faint gradient, box-shadow 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.4), color #f5f8fa, hover #30404d]; the caret `.bp3-html-select .bp3-icon, .bp3-select::after` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2]; the native dropdown options `.bp3-html-select option, .bp3-select option` follow the OS unless set [background #30404d, color #f5f8fa].\n  \xB7 Text input `.bp3-input` (also `textarea.bp3-input`): background #fff, box-shadow inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.15), inset 0 1px 1px rgba(16,22,26,.2), color #182026, `::placeholder` rgba(92,112,128,.6); `:focus` adds 0 0 0 1px #137cbd, 0 0 0 3px rgba(19,124,189,.3) [background rgba(16,22,26,.3), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.3), inset 0 1px 1px rgba(16,22,26,.4), color #f5f8fa, placeholder rgba(167,182,194,.6)]. Icons of input groups `.bp3-input-group .bp3-icon` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2].\n  \xB7 Checkbox / radio / switch: label `.bp3-control` text #182026 [#f5f8fa]; box `.bp3-control .bp3-control-indicator` #f5f8fa + gradient, inset shadow, hover #ebf1f5 [#394b59 + faint gradient, box-shadow 0 0 0 1px rgba(16,22,26,.4)]; checked `.bp3-control input:checked ~ .bp3-control-indicator` #137cbd (hover #106ba3) in both modes. Switch track `.bp3-control.bp3-switch input ~ .bp3-control-indicator` rgba(167,182,194,.5) [rgba(16,22,26,.5)], checked #137cbd, knob `.bp3-control.bp3-switch .bp3-control-indicator::before` white [#394b59].\n  \xB7 Tabs `.bp3-tab` #182026; selected and hover `.bp3-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"], .bp3-tab:not([aria-disabled=\"true\"]):hover` #106ba3 with underline box-shadow inset 0 -3px 0 #106ba3; `.bp3-tab-indicator` #106ba3 [text #f5f8fa, selected #48aff0].\n  \xB7 Blueprint badges `.bp3-tag` (hotkey hints, filter chips; NOT Roam #tags, which are `.rm-page-ref--tag`): #5c7080 text #f5f8fa [#bfccd6 / #182026]; `.bp3-tag.bp3-minimal` rgba(138,155,168,.2) text #182026 [text #f5f8fa].\n  \xB7 Menu `.bp3-menu` #fff / #182026 [#30404d / #f5f8fa]; `.bp3-menu-item:hover` rgba(167,182,194,.3) [rgba(138,155,168,.15)]; `.bp3-menu-item.bp3-active, .bp3-menu-item:active` rgba(115,134,148,.3); item icons `.bp3-menu-item > .bp3-icon` and labels `.bp3-menu-item-label` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2]; `.bp3-menu-divider` and `.bp3-menu-header` border-top rgba(16,22,26,.15) [rgba(255,255,255,.15)]; `.bp3-menu-header > h6` #182026 [#f5f8fa].\n  \xB7 Popover `.bp3-popover .bp3-popover-content` #fff, color inherit [#30404d]; its arrow is an SVG, `.bp3-popover .bp3-popover-arrow-fill { fill: #fff }` [#30404d]: forgetting it leaves a white triangle under a dark popover. Tooltip `.bp3-tooltip .bp3-popover-content` #394b59 / #f5f8fa in both modes.\n  \xB7 Dialog `.bp3-dialog` #ebf1f5 [#293742, color #f5f8fa]; `.bp3-dialog-header` #fff, box-shadow 0 1px 0 rgba(16,22,26,.15), its icons #5c7080 [#30404d, rgba(16,22,26,.4), icons #a7b6c2]; `.bp3-dialog-body` and `.bp3-dialog-footer` inherit; `.bp3-overlay-backdrop` rgba(16,22,26,.7).\n  \xB7 Also `.bp3-card` #fff [#30404d], `.bp3-heading` #182026 [#f5f8fa], `.bp3-text-muted` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2], `.bp3-text-disabled` rgba(92,112,128,.6) [rgba(167,182,194,.6)], `.bp3-form-group .bp3-form-helper-text` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2], `.bp3-divider` rgba(16,22,26,.15) [rgba(16,22,26,.4)], `.bp3-navbar` #fff [#394b59], `.bp3-editable-text.bp3-editable-text-editing::before` #fff [rgba(16,22,26,.3)], `.bp3-key` and kbd #fff / #5c7080 [#394b59 / #a7b6c2], plain links `a` #106ba3 [#48aff0]. Blueprint icons are SVGs filled with currentColor: set `color` on the icon, its button or its menu item. Icons inside buttons are tinted in BOTH modes by `.bp3-button .bp3-icon, .bp3-button .bp3-icon-standard, .bp3-button .bp3-icon-large { color: #5c7080 }`: to give every UI icon one tint, restyle them in light mode too, not only under the dark class. Many buttons and menu items carry their icon as a CLASS on the element itself (e.g. `<button class=\"bp3-button bp3-minimal bp3-icon-build\">`, used by Roam and by extensions such as SmartBlocks): the icon is then a font glyph drawn in `::before`, colored by `.bp3-button[class*=\"bp3-icon-\"]::before` and `.bp3-menu-item::before` (#5c7080 [#a7b6c2]), which rules on `.bp3-icon` children never reach: include `.bp3-button[class*=\"bp3-icon-\"]::before` and `.bp3-menu-item::before` in any icon rule.\n  \xB7 SPECIFICITY TRAP: Blueprint's base selectors already weigh 2 or 3 classes (`.bp3-button:not([class*=\"bp3-intent-\"])` = 0,2,0; its `:hover` = 0,3,0; `.bp3-button.bp3-minimal:hover` = 0,3,0; `.bp3-input:focus` = 0,2,0; `.bp3-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"]` = 0,2,0). So `.rm-dark-theme .bp3-button { \u2026 }` (0,2,0) only wins at rest and the button flashes back to its LIGHT hover color. Either mirror Blueprint's selectors exactly (`.rm-dark-theme .bp3-button:not([class*=\"bp3-intent-\"])`, `\u2026:hover`, `\u2026:active, \u2026.bp3-active`, `\u2026:disabled, \u2026.bp3-disabled`, `.rm-dark-theme .bp3-button.bp3-minimal:hover`, `.rm-dark-theme .bp3-input:focus`\u2026) or put `!important` on the dark declarations. And ALWAYS neutralise the light gradient: declare `background-image: none` (or the `background:` shorthand) together with `background-color`, otherwise the white gradient stays painted over the dark color and the control looks washed out.\n  \xB7 MORE BLUEPRINT & ROAM POPUPS (verified 2026-09-24 against blueprint.css, blueprint-datetime.css and site.css). Each is LIGHT by default and stays light under `.rm-dark-theme` unless restyled; their text inherits the page color, so a dark theme that forgets them shows light text on white: date picker `.bp3-datepicker` #fff [#30404d], days `.bp3-datepicker .DayPicker-Day` inherit the text color, `:hover` #d8e1e8 / #182026 [#5c7080 / #fff], `.DayPicker-Day--selected` #137cbd white, `.DayPicker-Day--outside` and `.DayPicker-WeekNumber` rgba(92,112,128,.6) [rgba(167,182,194,.6)], footer `.bp3-datepicker-footer`; Roam's own jump-to-date picker `.rm-jump-date-picker` adds `.DayPicker-Day--today` #137CBD, `.DayPicker-Day--dateHasNoPage` #5C7080, selected #5C7080 / #F5F8FA; time picker `.bp3-timepicker .bp3-timepicker-input-row` #fff with inset shadow, `.bp3-timepicker-input` #182026. Toasts `.bp3-toast` #fff with shadow, icon `.bp3-toast > .bp3-icon` #5c7080 [#394b59, icon #a7b6c2] (intent toasts `.bp3-toast.bp3-intent-*` are colored with white text in both modes: keep them). Alerts `.bp3-alert` are `.bp3-dialog`s (body `.bp3-alert-body`, footer `.bp3-alert-footer`). Keys `.bp3-key` #fff / #5c7080 with a light shadow [#394b59 / #a7b6c2]. Blueprint callouts `.bp3-callout` rgba(138,155,168,.15), icon #5c7080 [rgba(138,155,168,.2)]. Labels `label.bp3-label` inherit [#f5f8fa]; helper text `.bp3-form-group .bp3-form-helper-text` #5c7080 [#a7b6c2]. Drawer `.bp3-drawer` #fff [#30404d]. Omnibar `.bp3-omnibar` #fff [#30404d]. Tables `table.bp3-html-table` th/td #182026 [#f5f8fa]. Sliders: handle `.bp3-slider-handle` like a button, track `.bp3-slider-progress` rgba(92,112,128,.2) [rgba(16,22,26,.5)]. Tooltips need no change (dark in both modes).\n  \xB7 SEARCH & COMMAND PALETTE (site.css): the search dialog (Ctrl/Cmd+U, top bar search) is `.rm-find-or-create-modal` (#ffffff, radius 8px, inside `.rm-modal-portal--find-or-create > .bp3-overlay > .bp3-dialog-container > .bp3-dialog`) > `.rm-find-or-create-modal-header` (border-bottom #E5E6E5; query input `.rm-find-or-create-modal-header__query-input.bp3-input` transparent; icon `__left-icon` #5C7080), results `.rm-find-or-create-modal-body__list > li.bp3-menu-item` (active `.bp3-active` #E1E8ED), rows `.rm-find-or-create-row__snippet` #182026, `__breadcrumb` #738694, `__ref-count` #8A9BA8, `__icon` #5C7080, `__label` #15803d, group headers `.rm-find-or-create-body__group-header`, preview pane `.rm-find-or-create-modal-preview` (border-left #E5E6E5, title #A7B6C2), footer `.rm-find-or-create-footer` #ebeceb with border-top #D3D4D4 (title #5C7080, action hover #DFE0DF, hotkey icons `__action-hotkey-icon` rgba(0,0,0,.08)); the inline search popover of the top bar is `.rm-find-or-create-popover` with menu `.rm-find-or-create__menu`. FOOTER (added recently, often forgotten by themes; live DOM 2026-09-24): both the modal and the top bar search popover `.rm-find-or-create-popover` (> `ul.bp3-menu.rm-find-or-create__menu` with `li.rm-find-or-create-body__group-header` (#738694, 11px/600) and rows `li.bp3-menu-item` > `.rm-find-or-create-row` > `.rm-find-or-create-row__icon.bp3-icon` + `.rm-find-or-create-row__title` (500, inherits its color) > `sup.rm-find-or-create-row__ref-count`; a BLOCK result is `.rm-find-or-create-row.rm-find-or-create-row--block` > `.rm-find-or-create-row__block` > [`.rm-find-or-create-row__breadcrumb` > `.bp3-overflow-list.rm-zoom-path` > `.rm-zoom-item` > `.rm-find-or-create-row__breadcrumb-segment`, then `.rm-find-or-create-row__snippet`]; the selected row is `li.bp3-menu-item.bp3-active` (#E1E8ED, mouse hover transparent by design). These surfaces are white in LIGHT mode too: a theme with a tinted light background should restyle the popover, its menu and the active row in both modes, not only under the dark class) end with `.rm-find-or-create-footer` (#ebeceb, border-top #D3D4D4, 12px; 10px in the popover) > `.rm-find-or-create-footer__title` (#5C7080) + `.rm-find-or-create-footer__actions` > buttons `button.bp3-button.bp3-minimal.rm-find-or-create-footer__action` (hover #DFE0DF; `--toggle` = the Preview toggle, hidden in the modal; `--active` = toggled on, #D3D4D4; `--primary` = Open, bold `__action-desc`) separated by `.bp3-divider`, each holding `.rm-find-or-create-footer__action-desc` and `.rm-find-or-create-footer__action-hotkey` > `.rm-find-or-create-footer__action-hotkey-icon` (key badges rgba(0,0,0,.08), as text spans or `.bp3-icon-key-enter` SVGs; transparent inside an `--active` button). TRAP: the footer actions ARE minimal Blueprint buttons, so a theme rule for `.bp3-button.bp3-minimal` (e.g. `.rm-dark-theme .bp3-button.bp3-minimal:not([class*=\"bp3-intent-\"])`, 0,4,0) overrides Roam's `.rm-find-or-create-footer__action--active.bp3-button` (0,2,0) and erases the toggled state: restyle `--active` (and its :hover) explicitly with a stronger selector such as `.rm-find-or-create-footer__actions > .rm-find-or-create-footer__action--active.bp3-button.bp3-minimal`. The multi-graph search has the same footer as `.rm-cross-graph-search-footer` (`__action-items__action-item`, `__hotkey__icon` #D3D4D4). Command palette (Ctrl/Cmd+P): `.rm-command-palette` (a `.bp3-dialog`), menu `.rm-command-palette__menu` with items `.rm-menu-item` (active `.rm-menu-item--active` #d5dadf), shortcut badges `.rm-command-palette__shortcut` #d5dadf, footer `.rm-command-palette__footer` #ebeceb. Roam's dark values for all these: surfaces var(--dark-bg-2), footers var(--dark-bg) with border #5C7080 and text #A7B6C2, active items var(--dark-hl), secondary text #A7B6C2, snippet var(--dark-ff).\n  \xB7 `.rm-settings` (Roam's Settings dialog) is dark by design even in light mode (#202B33 background and inputs, #293742 menus, popovers and section borders, text #E1E8ED): do not lighten it and do not take it as the reference for other dialogs.\n- Default light-mode values: page links `.rm-page-ref--link` #106BA3, tags `.rm-page-ref--tag` #A7B6C2, bullets `.rm-bullet__inner` #394B59 (4px transparent border, 50% radius), thread line `.rm-multibar` border #BFCCD6, block refs `.rm-block-ref` no background, a .5px #D8E1E8 bottom border and #F5F8FA only on :hover, blockquotes `.rm-bq` background #F5F8FA with a 4px #30404D left border, code blocks `.rm-code-block` background #f5f5f5, autocomplete `.rm-autocomplete__results` white, right sidebar `#right-sidebar` background rgba(92,112,128,0.05), queries `.rm-query` .5px #BFCCD6 border, inline references panel `.rm-inline-references` (opened under a block by its reference counter `.rm-block__ref-count`) #F5F8FA. Query titles `.rm-query .rm-query-title` (and the search page header `.rm-search-query-header`) take background var(--background-color) and color var(--primary-color): these two Roam variables are the way to theme them (--background-color is used nowhere else in site.css). Reference items `.rm-reference-item` (linked references AND query results) hsl(204,33%,97%); nested matches `.rm-nested-matches` #E1E8ED; page embeds `.rm-embed--page` and `.rm-embed-path` #EBF1F5; block-ref parentheses `.rm-paren` #F5F8FA with a 1px #EBF1F5 border (`.rm-paren__paren` #738694, `.rm-paren--closed:hover` #CED9E0 / #182026); horizontal outline children `.roam-article .rm-level-horizontal-outline__child` white; kanban board `.kanban-board` #A7B6C2 (see KANBAN below); selection highlights `.block-highlight-blue` #7cccff and `.block-highlight-grey` #CED9E0. The breadcrumb path of a zoomed block ends with a mask `.rm-zoom.zoom-path-view .rm-zoom-mask { mix-blend-mode: saturation; background-color: white }` that bleaches whatever is under it on a dark or tinted background: set `background-color: unset` in dark mode. CodeMirror active line: `.cm-focused .cm-activeLineGutter { background-color: #e2f2ff !important }` (light blue even in dark mode unless restyled with !important).\n- DATA ATTRIBUTES set by Roam's renderer (the way to target ONE tag, page or family of them): a tag `.rm-page-ref--tag` carries `data-tag=\"<page name>\"` (without the #), a page link is NOT attributed itself: its markup is `<span data-link-title=\"<page name>\" data-link-uid=\"\u2026\"> <span class=\"rm-page-ref__brackets\">[[</span> <span class=\"rm-page-ref rm-page-ref--link\">name</span> <span class=\"rm-page-ref__brackets\">]]</span> </span>`, so the attribute sits on the class-less WRAPPER span and the link must be reached with a descendant selector: `[data-link-title=\"Inbox\"] .rm-page-ref--link` (never `.rm-page-ref--link[data-link-title=\u2026]`, which matches nothing). Every block container `.roam-block-container` carries `data-page-links='[\"<page>\", \u2026]'` listing the pages referenced in that block (tags, links, attributes, TODO/DONE), and `data-path-page-links` for the pages referenced by its ancestors. So: one tag `.rm-page-ref--tag[data-tag=\"urgent\"]`; a family of tags `.rm-page-ref--tag[data-tag^=\"project/\"]` (`^=` starts with, `*=` contains, `$=` ends with); one page link `[data-link-title=\"Inbox\"] .rm-page-ref--link`; page links starting with \"test\" `[data-link-title^=\"test\"] .rm-page-ref--link` (their brackets: `[data-link-title^=\"test\"] .rm-page-ref__brackets`); a whole block tagged with it `.roam-block-container[data-page-links*='\"urgent\"'] > .rm-block-main` (the block row, excluding the children; DONE blocks are `[data-page-links*='\"DONE\"']`). Page names are case-sensitive; a name with spaces or quotes must be quoted. Never use `display: none` on a block container (hide at most the tag span itself). An icon before a tag: `.rm-page-ref--tag[data-tag^=\"idea\"]::before { content: \"\uD83D\uDCA1 \"; }`.\n- Selector families in Roam's stylesheet: `rm-*` (most UI), `roam-*` (app shell, blocks, sidebars, log), Blueprint `bp3-*` (buttons, menus, popovers, dialogs, inputs), `kanban-*`, `starred-pages`, `check-container`, `log-button`. Callouts are `.rm-callout`, `.rm-callout__header`, `.rm-callout__body`, `.rm-callout--note|info|tip|warning|danger|example|quote\u2026`. Native tables (not {{table}}) are `.rm-table`, `.rm-table__cell`.\n- BLOCK ANATOMY (live DOM, 2026-09-24): `.roam-block-container` (also `.rm-block`, `.block-bullet-view`) > `.rm-block-main` (the SAME element is also `.rm-block__self`) > [`.rm-block__controls` (`span.block-expand` > `.rm-caret`, then `.rm-bullet` > `.bp3-popover-wrapper` > \u2026 `.rm-bullet__inner`), then ONE content div classed `.rm-block__input.rm-block__input--view.roam-block.rm-block-text` (the classes are on the same element, never chain them as descendants) whose children are the rendered spans, then `.rm-block-separator`] + `.rm-block-children.rm-block__children.rm-level-N` (N = depth, `.rm-level-0` = top-level blocks of the page) > `.rm-multibar` + child containers. A block whose content is a component (code block, native table, embed) has NO `.rm-block-text` class: to reach every block use `.roam-block` (the most inclusive) or `.rm-block__input`. A block holding a table also gets `.rm-block__self--horizontal-scroller` on its `.rm-block-main`. EDITING (live DOM): the content div is replaced by `.rm-autocomplete__wrapper` > `textarea.rm-block-input.rm-block__input.rm-block__input--active.rm-block-text` and the container gets `.rm-focused` instead of `.rm-not-focused`. So a rule on `.rm-block__input` or `.rm-block-text` ALSO styles the textarea (keep it readable), while `.roam-block` only matches the rendered (view mode) text. State classes on the container: `.rm-block--open` / `.rm-block--closed` (collapsed, bullet gets `.rm-bullet--closed`), `.rm-block--editable`, `.rm-block--mine` / `.rm-block--others`, `.rm-not-focused`; on the caret: `.rm-caret-open` / `.rm-caret-closed`, plus `.rm-caret-hidden` / `.rm-caret-showing` (visible on hover). Besides `data-page-links` / `data-path-page-links`, the container carries `data-block-uid` (target ONE block: `.roam-block-container[data-block-uid=\"abc123XYZ\"] > .rm-block-main`), `data-page-title`, `data-create-display-name` / `data-edit-display-name` (author, e.g. to tint the blocks of one collaborator) and `data-create-time` / `data-edit-time`.\n- HEADINGS: `.rm-heading-level-1/2/3` is set on the BLOCK CONTAINER (`.roam-block-container`), not on the text, so it is inherited by every child block: target the heading text only with `.rm-heading-level-1 > .rm-block-main .rm-block__input` (Roam's own rule is `.rm-heading-level-1 > .rm-block__self .rm-block__input`, same element), never `.rm-heading-level-1 .rm-block-text`. Defaults: H1 1.8em/400, H2 1.4em/400, H3 1.2em/500 #5C7080; Roam also keeps the older text classes `.rm-level1/2/3` for the same sizes. FONT TRAP: Roam sets `font-family: \"Inter\", sans-serif` on H1 and `font-family: \"Inter\", sans-serif !important` on H2 (`.rm-heading-level-2 > .rm-block__self .rm-block__input`), so a theme font for headings needs `!important`, at least for H2.\n- INLINE PARTS (live DOM): TODO/DONE checkbox `span.rm-checkbox.rm-todo` > `label.check-container` > `input[type=checkbox]` + `span.checkmark` (the visible box is `.checkmark`); strikethrough ~~\u2026~~ is `.rm-strikethrough`; page title `.rm-title-display-container[data-page-uid]` > `h1.rm-title-display` > span (36px/500 #202b33). INLINE CODE `code` is styled by Roam's bundled re-com.min.css (`code { color: #333; background: #eee; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 4px; padding: .1em .3em }`, Menlo 90% from bootstrap), not by site.css: it stays light in a `.rm-dark-theme` theme unless restyled (`.rm-block__input code`).\n- INLINE ELEMENTS (live DOM): strikethrough is `del.rm-strikethrough`; external alias `a.rm-alias.rm-alias--external` (inside a `.bp3-popover-wrapper`, default #106ba3 with an underline border of the same color); attribute name `span.rm-attr-ref[data-link-uid]` (no data-link-title: an attribute cannot be targeted by name); inline image `.rm-inline-img` inside `.rm-inline-img__resize`.\n- QUERY anatomy (live DOM): `.rm-query.rm-full-width` > [`.rm-query-title` (`.rm-caret`, `.rm-query-title-text` > `.rm-query-title-input`, minimal buttons incl. `.rm-query__refresh-button`), `.rm-reference-main.rm-query-content` > `.rm-mentions.refs-by-page-view` > `.rm-ref-page-view`\u2026]. Query results REUSE the linked references markup, so `.rm-reference-main`, `.rm-ref-page-view`, `.rm-reference-item` rules also restyle every query: scope page references with `.rm-reference-wrapper > .rm-reference-main` and query results with `.rm-query-content`.\n- CALLOUT anatomy: `.rm-block__input` > `.rm-callout.rm-callout--<type>` > `.rm-callout__header` (`.bp3-popover-wrapper` > \u2026 `.rm-callout__icon.bp3-icon`, then `.rm-callout__title`) + `.rm-callout__body`. Types seen: note, info, tip, important, warning, success, question, example (also abstract/summary/tldr, todo, check/done, help/faq, caution/attention, failure/fail/missing, danger/error, bug, quote/cite); each sets `--callout-color` and `--_callout-bg` (background = `var(--callout-bg, var(--_callout-bg))`, so a theme may set `--callout-bg`).\n- CODE BLOCK anatomy: `.rm-block__input` > span > `.rm-inline-code-block` > `.rm-code-block.rm-code-block--<language>` (background #f5f5f5) > div > CodeMirror 6 `.cm-editor` > `.cm-scroller` > `.cm-gutters` (line numbers) + `.cm-content` (the code, `.cm-line` per line); cursor and selection layers `.cm-cursorLayer`, `.cm-selectionLayer`; syntax tokens are `.cmt-*` classes (`.cmt-keyword`, `.cmt-string`, `.cmt-number`, `.cmt-comment`, `.cmt-propertyName`\u2026); toolbar `.rm-code-block__settings-bar` with `.rm-code-block__language-chooser`. It is NOT CodeMirror 5: `.cm-s-default` / `.CodeMirror` match nothing.\n- LAYOUT STATE classes on `.rm-article-wrapper`: `.rm-spacing--small|medium|large|full` (page width setting), `.rm-spacing--left-sidebar-open`, `.rm-spacing--right-sidebar-open|closed`. Use them to adapt widths to the sidebars.\n- LEFT SIDEBAR: `.roam-sidebar-container` > `.roam-sidebar-content` > entries `.log-button` (each holds a `.flex-h-box` with an icon GLYPH span `span.bp3-icon-small.bp3-icon-<name>.icon`, not a `.bp3-icon` element, colored hsl(204,20%,45%) by `.roam-body .roam-app .roam-sidebar-container .roam-sidebar-content .icon`) also classed `.rm-left-sidebar__daily-notes`, `.rm-left-sidebar__graph-overview`, `.rm-left-sidebar__all-pages`, `.rm-left-sidebar__roam-depot`; the graph name is `.rm-db-title`; shortcuts are `.starred-pages-wrapper` > `.starred-pages` > `a` > `.page` (one per shortcut). Default: sidebar background #182026 (dark even in light mode), entries #5c778a 16px/500. Hover backgrounds are #10161A on `.top-row`, `.log-button`, shortcuts `.starred-pages .page` (each under `.roam-body .roam-app .roam-sidebar-container .roam-sidebar-content`, specificity 0,6,0) and on the Roam logo row at the bottom `#roam-sidebar-logo:hover` (an ID selector): a theme with a light sidebar must override all four (with `!important` for the logo row). The graph name opens the graph dropdown `.rm-graph-dropdown` (links `a` #182026, `.menu-title` #8A9BA8, `.menu-item`, settings row `.setting` #EBF1F5, hover #CED9E0); the graph name `.rm-db-title-container .rm-db-title` #CED9E0 and its `.expand-icon` #5c7080; the shortcuts header `.starred-pages-wrapper` #5C7080.\n- DAILY NOTES LOG (the chronological list of recent daily notes, route #/app/<graph> without a page; live DOM 2026-09-24): `.roam-article` > `.roam-log-container` (also `.flex-v-box`) > one `.roam-log-page` per day, each holding in order: `.rm-title-display-container[data-page-uid]` > `h1.rm-title-display` (plain text, no <a>: the click is handled by script), then `.roam-title-day-banner` (a SIBLING after the title container, not a wrapper), then the day's blocks `.rm-block-children.rm-level-0`, then its own linked references `.rm-reference-wrapper` > `.rm-reference-main`. Titles in the log are 30px/500 #5c7080 (line-height 1.25), vs 36px/500 #202b33 on a single page: target them with `.roam-log-page .rm-title-display`. Roam's rules (site.css): days are separated by `.rm-article-wrapper .roam-log-container .roam-log-page { border-top: 1px solid #738694; margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px }` and the first day has none (`:first-child { border: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; min-height: 500px }`): these selectors weigh 0,3,0, so a theme changing the separator must use the same chain (or more). The last, not yet rendered day (below the fold) is a placeholder `.roam-log-page.roam-log-preview` > `.flex-h-box` > `h1.level2` (grey #8A9BA8, NOT a `.rm-title-display`): it is ALSO a `.roam-log-page`, so it gets the separator and every `.roam-log-page` rule; style its h1 too (`.roam-log-preview h1`) or it flashes in Roam's colors while scrolling. Block inputs of the log have ids starting with `block-input-log-outline-`. Target the log only with `.roam-log-container \u2026` (a single daily note opened as a page has no `.roam-log-container`).\n- LINKED REFERENCES anatomy (live DOM): `.rm-reference-wrapper` > `.rm-reference-main` > `.rm-reference-main__child-wrapper` > `.rm-reference-container` > `.rm-mentions.refs-by-page-view` (the LIST of linked references; `.rm-mentions-search` is its filter input, hidden until used) > one `.rm-ref-page-view` per referencing page > [`.rm-title-arrow-wrapper` (`.rm-caret` + `.rm-ref-page-view-title` > a > `.rm-page__title`, 16px #202b33), then the `.rm-reference-item` blocks, each preceded by its breadcrumb `.rm-zoom.zoom-mentions-view` (`.rm-zoom-item` #5c7080)]. Unlinked references are a separate `.rm-unlinked-reference-container` (collapsed by default).\n- RIGHT SIDEBAR anatomy (live DOM): `#right-sidebar` (background rgba(92,112,128,.05), i.e. #f7f8f9 over white) > `#roam-right-sidebar-content` > `.sidebar-content` > div > one `.rm-sidebar-window[data-sidebar-window-id]` per open window (its header and `.rm-sidebar-window__controls`) > `.rm-sidebar-outline-wrapper` > `.rm-sidebar-outline` > [breadcrumb `.rm-zoom.zoom-path-view` > `.rm-zoom-item` > `.rm-zoom-item-content`, then `.rm-zoom-block-wrapper` > the block tree]. Blocks in it are ordinary `.roam-block-container`s: scope sidebar-only rules with `#right-sidebar \u2026`. When it is open, `.rm-article-wrapper` gets `.rm-spacing--right-sidebar-open`.\n- BLOCK REFERENCE & EMBED anatomy (live DOM): a block ref is `span.rm-block-ref[data-uid][data-original-page-links]` (inside two `.bp3-popover-wrapper` > `.bp3-popover-target` layers; its content is ordinary rendered spans, links included): target refs to ONE block with `.rm-block-ref[data-uid=\"abc123XYZ\"]`; at rest it has no background, only its .5px #D8E1E8 bottom border. A block embed is `.rm-embed-container.rm-embed-container--block` > [`.rm-embed-settings` (minimal buttons), `.rm-embed-margin-action-edit`, `.rm-hide-bullet` > `.rm-embed-inner-block-hide` > (`.rm-embed-margin-action` + the embedded `.roam-block-container`)].\n- NATIVE TABLE defaults (site.css): the <table> is `.rm-table table { background: white }`; header cells are `.rm-table th { background: hsl(204,33%,97%); border: 1px solid #CED9E0; font-weight: 600 }` (specificity 0,1,1: a theme rule `.rm-table th { background: \u2026 }` wins by source order, no need for extra specificity); body cells `.rm-table td { border: 1px solid #CED9E0 }`. `.rm-table__cell` is the content WRAPPER inside each th/td (padding 4px 8px, overflow hidden), so a background set on it does not cover the whole cell: set cell backgrounds and borders on `.rm-table th` / `.rm-table td`, and use `.rm-table__cell` for the inner padding. Roam's own dark values: table #293742, th rgba(255,255,255,.05), borders #394B59.\n- NATIVE TABLE anatomy (live DOM): `.rm-block__input` > span > span > `.rm-table` > [`.rm-table__resize-handles` > `.rm-table__resize-handle`, `table` > `tbody` > `tr` > `th` / `td` > `.rm-table__cell`, `.rm-table__add-row-btn`, `.rm-table__add-col-btn`]. The header row is made of `th` INSIDE `tbody` (no `thead` observed), so style headers with `.rm-table th`, never `.rm-table thead th`. Every cell carries `data-row` and `data-col` (0-based): first column `.rm-table td[data-col=\"0\"]`, second row `.rm-table [data-row=\"1\"]`. ZEBRA ROWS: set the background on the cells, both parities explicitly, and in dark mode also repaint the table itself (Roam paints `.rm-table table` white): `.rm-table tr:nth-child(odd) > td { background-color: <A> }` `.rm-table tr:nth-child(even) > td { background-color: <B> }` plus the same two rules under `.rm-dark-theme` and `.rm-dark-theme .rm-table table { background: <dark> }` (the first tr is the header row of th cells, so `> td` rules never touch it; data-row parity cannot be matched with an attribute selector). Setting the background on `.rm-table__cell` only paints the inner padding box, not the whole cell. Header pills `.rm-table__col-pill` / `.rm-table__row-pill` (targets `*-pill-target`), `.rm-table__selection-overlay`.\n- KANBAN anatomy ({{kanban}}, live DOM 2026-09-25) and site.css defaults: `.kanban-board` (#A7B6C2, padding 12px) > `.kanban-column-container` (flex, overflow-x scroll) > one `.kanban-column` per column (flex 1 0 200px, #ededed, margin 4px, padding 4px, cursor pointer) > [`.kanban-title` > span (centered, FIXED min-height and max-height 40px, so long titles are cut, padding 4px 0 8px, margin-bottom 12px, border-bottom 1px solid #5C7080), then alternating `.rm-dnd-separator` (8px drop zones; while dragging `.rm-dnd-drop-area > .rm-dnd-drop-bar` 5px #5C7080) and `.kanban-card` (draggable, white, margin 0 8px, padding 8px) > the card's block content `.rm-block__input.roam-block.rm-block-text`, replaced by a textarea while editing (`.kanban-card textarea`)]. Roam's dark values: board var(--dark-left-bg), columns var(--dark-bg), cards and their textarea var(--dark-bg-2). To restyle titles, reset `min-height`/`max-height` and `border-bottom`; column order is reachable with `.kanban-column:nth-child(n)`.\n- DIAGRAM ({{diagram}}, React Flow; live DOM and site.css 2026-09-25): `.rm-diagram` (`.rm-diagram-full-screen` when maximized) carries its colors as CSS variables in an INLINE style, which are ALSO the per-diagram settings the user edits in its Properties panel: `--diagram-background-color: white; --block-fill-color: white; --block-text-color: black; --block-border-color: #A7B6C2; --edge-stroke-color / --global-edge-stroke-color: #A7B6C2; --group-border-color: #A7B6C2; --group-title-text-color: black; --group-title-fill-color: #A7B6C23F; --group-area-fill-color: rgba(225, 232, 237, 0.2)` (defaults). To theme only the defaults and keep the user's choices, match the inline value and redeclare the variable with !important: `.rm-diagram[style*=\"--block-fill-color: white\"] { --block-fill-color: \u2026 !important }`. Arrow heads are `<marker style=\"stroke: rgb(167, 182, 194); fill: \u2026\">` (inline). Nodes `.react-flow__node-block` (hover and `.selected:after` glow box-shadow #CED9E0) > `.rm-parsed-block-string`; groups `.react-flow__node-group` (title `.rm-node-group__title-inner-wrapper`); edges `.react-flow__edge-path`. Chrome with a hard-coded WHITE background (text inherits, so unreadable in a dark theme): the Properties panel `.rm-diagram .rm-diagram-properties-panel` (header `__header`, sections, `--disabled`), the title panel `.rm-diagram-title-panel` (input `.rm-diagram-title`), the node toolbar `.rm-diagram .react-flow__node-toolbar`, the pane context menu `.rm-diagram-pane-context-menu`, the minimap `.react-flow__minimap` (nodes `.react-flow__minimap-node` fill #BFCCD6 and mask `.react-flow__minimap-mask`, both SVG attributes that a CSS `fill` overrides), and React Flow's controls `.react-flow__controls` > `.react-flow__controls-button` (#fefefe, hover #f4f4f4, border-bottom #eee; SVG icons need `fill: currentColor`, other icons are `.bp3-icon-standard` glyph spans). Background dots `.react-flow__background circle` fill #91919a; resize handle `.rm-diagram-node__resize-control` white.\n- STREAK ({{streak: [[page]]}}, a GitHub-like contribution grid; live DOM and site.css 2026-09-25): `.rm-streak` > [div > `span.rm-streak__title` (\"Streak for [[page]]\", 500) + a minimal info button, then `.rm-streak__grid` (CSS grid, columns max-content + 55 \xD7 12px, rows max-content + 7 \xD7 12px, 1px gaps) > `.rm-streak__weekday` (Mon/Wed/Fri/Sun, 12px, padding-right 5px) and `.rm-streak__month` (12px, padding-bottom 3px) labels, both inheriting the text color, then one `.rm-streak__day.rm-streak__day-N` per day (border-radius 1px, placed by an INLINE `grid-area`, with a `title` tooltip \"Mon Oct 20, 2025: 2 times\")]; an error is `.rm-streak__error` (red). N is the intensity 0 to 4. Light defaults `.rm-streak__day-0` #EBEDF0, `-1` #9BE9A8, `-2` #41C464, `-3` #2FA14E, `-4` #206E39; Roam's dark values exist only under `.bp3-dark` (#2d333b, #0e4429, #006d32, #26a641, #39d353), so under `.rm-dark-theme` the empty days stay light grey (#EBEDF0) on the dark page unless restyled. Theme the five levels together as a ramp from the empty color to the accent, e.g. `.rm-streak .rm-streak__day-2 { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, var(--empty)) }` (`.rm-streak .rm-streak__day-N`, 0,2,0, also beats `.bp3-dark .rm-streak__day-N` by source order); never resize the cells or change the grid tracks (the 12px tracks are fixed and the cells are positioned inline).\n- DATALOG QUERY TABLES ({{datalog query}} / Datomic queries, not native tables): `.rm-ds-q` (header `.rm-ds-q__header` 600, errors `.rm-ds-q__error` red, warnings `.rm-ds-q__warning`) > `.rm-data-table` > [`.rm-data-table__header`, `.rm-data-table__table` > table: header cells `th` holding `.rm-column-header.rm-column-header--real` (> `.rm-column-header__name`, sortable, hover rgba(167,182,194,.2)) and one `.rm-column-header--fake`; body cells `td.rm-data-table__table__cell-container` (`--roam-entity-view` when the cell renders a block, with `.rm-data-table__table__custom-cell--render-block` inside), `.rm-data-table__footer`]. Roam's defaults (site.css): `.rm-data-table__table th, .rm-data-table__table td, .rm-data-table__table tr { font-size: 12px; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid grey }` (th padding 0), NO background anywhere and NO dark variant: in a dark theme they inherit the page background, and the `grey` borders must be restyled. Zebra rows: `.rm-data-table__table tbody tr:nth-child(even) > td`. Its settings (gear) menu is a Blueprint menu `ul.bp3-menu.rm-data-table.rm-data-table__settings` in a `.bp3-portal` popover, with switches, a `.rm-numeric-input` and `.rm-sorting-button`s (inactive sort icons `.rm-sorting-button--inactive .bp3-icon` lightgray).\n- HARD-CODED LIGHT VALUES often missed by dark themes (verified 2026-09-25): All Pages titles `.rm-pages-title-text { color: black }` (title column `.rm-all-pages .table .rm-pages-row .rm-pages-title-col` #BFCCD6); the Graph Overview settings panel `.rm-graph-view-control-panel` #fff (open state `--open` has its own box-shadow; it holds minimal buttons, a `.bp3-button.bp3-fill` and `.bp3-control.bp3-switch`es); the help popup search `.rm-help-search__icon-container` + `.rm-help-search__input` (white input, border #B4B7BB); left sidebar entry icons are glyph spans `.roam-sidebar-content .icon` (hsl(204,20%,45%), selector weight 0,5,0), not `.bp3-icon`. The [[ / # / / autocomplete `.rm-autocomplete__results` paints its selected row with an INLINE style `background-color: rgb(213, 218, 223)` and its key hint with `color: rgb(129, 145, 157)`: only an attribute selector with !important reaches them, e.g. `.rm-autocomplete__results [style*=\"background-color: rgb(213, 218, 223)\"] { background-color: \u2026 !important }`. The autocomplete also has a preview pane `.rm-autocomplete__preview` (white, border-left #D3D4D4) and a footer `.rm-autocomplete-footer` (#ebeceb, border-top #D3D4D4, actions `.rm-autocomplete-footer__action--active` #D3D4D4 and `--preview:hover` #DFE0DF, key badges `.rm-autocomplete-footer__action__hotkey__icon` rgba(0,0,0,.08)). The bullet context menu (right click on a bullet) is `.bp3-menu.bp3-text-small` whose alignment / heading / view buttons carry an INLINE white `background-color`: Roam's own dark mode overrides them with `.bp3-menu.bp3-text-small button[style*=\"background-color\"] { \u2026 !important }` and their icons `.bp3-menu.bp3-text-small button .bp3-icon-standard`. Minimal button groups `.bp3-button-group.bp3-minimal .bp3-button:hover, :active, .bp3-active` force text #182026 (dark on dark). Native table column menu `.rm-table .rm-table__col-menu` (items `.rm-table__col-menu-item`, hover rgba(0,0,0,.05), active #106BA3, divider `.rm-table__col-menu-divider` #CED9E0), pills `.rm-table__col-pill` / `.rm-table__row-pill` borders. Sidebar search window `.rm-sidebar-search > div` (Roam's dark rule uses !important). Search filter chips `.rm-search-filter-chip` #5C7080 (hover #E1E8ED, `--active` #137CBD white, `--add` dashed #BFCCD6). Placeholders and empty titles `.rm-title-untitled`, `.rm-input::placeholder`, `.rm-title-textarea::placeholder` #CED9E0. Other hard-coded grey TEXT to re-tint with the theme's muted colors: `.rm-autocomplete__ref-count` #8A9BA8, `.rm-autocomplete__preview-title` and `__preview-placeholder` #A7B6C2, `.rm-block__self .rm-block__ref-count.rm-active` #8A9BA8, `.rm-table__ref-count` #A7B6C2, `.rm-table__add-row-btn:hover` / `__add-col-btn:hover` #5C7080, `.rm-table__empty-filter-cell` #8A9BA8, `.rm-query-builder-popover .bp3-menu-header` #8A9BA8, `.rm-command-palette__menu--empty` #8A9BA8, All Pages headers and sorting (`.rm-pages-row-header`, `.sorted-header-text`, `.sort-button.focused`, `.toolbar-search-group .search-icon`) #BFCCD6 / #5C7080, `.rm-pages-title-text.title-children-text` #BFCCD6, `.rm-filtered-out` #CED9E0, `.rm-graph-icons` #738694, `.rm-grey-text` #8A9BA8.\n- SCROLLBARS (site.css 2026-09-25): Roam HIDES vertical scrollbars everywhere with a global `::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 0px; max-height: 4px; background: transparent }` (horizontal ones are 4px high at most); `.rm-hide-scrollbar` hides them explicitly (`display: none`, keep it); the Settings dialog, Roam Depot and the PDF viewer have their own 8px scrollbars (thumb #8A9BA8). Roam ALSO loads re-com.min.css (verified 2026-09-25), whose global rules are MORE SPECIFIC than a plain pseudo-element: `::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 10px; background-color: rgba(0,0,0,.05) }`, `::-webkit-scrollbar:horizontal { height: 10px }` (0,1,1), `::-webkit-scrollbar:hover { background-color: rgba(0,0,0,.2) }`, `::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:horizontal, ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:vertical { background: rgba(0,0,0,.25); border-radius: 5px }` (0,1,1: the GREY thumb) and `\u2026:active` rgba(0,0,0,.45). So a theme rule on `::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb` (0,0,1) is silently ignored: ALWAYS write `::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:vertical, ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:horizontal` (with `:hover` / `:active` variants), size horizontal bars on `::-webkit-scrollbar:horizontal` (`height` and `max-height`), vertical ones on `::-webkit-scrollbar` (`width`), and reset the track on `::-webkit-scrollbar, ::-webkit-scrollbar:hover { background: transparent }`, plus `::-webkit-scrollbar-track` and `::-webkit-scrollbar-corner` (transparent). Use the `background` shorthand (re-com does) and repeat `background-clip: padding-box` after it. Slim and elegant: width 8px, thumb with `border: 2px solid transparent; background-clip: padding-box; border-radius: 8px` (a 4px visible thumb, `border-width: 1px` on hover); horizontal bars THINNER than vertical ones (`::-webkit-scrollbar:horizontal { height: 6px; max-height: 6px }`, `::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:horizontal { border-width: 1.5px }`, a 3px thumb). COLOR: a neutral grey or the plain muted text color reads as default browser grey; tint the thumb with the theme's accent, discreetly (e.g. `color-mix(in srgb, <accent> 35%, <border color>)`, 70% on hover), and use the sidebar's own accent on the left sidebar (`.roam-sidebar-container ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb`). TRAP: in Chromium 121+ (Chrome, Edge, the Roam desktop app), setting the standard `scrollbar-width` or `scrollbar-color` on an element makes it IGNORE every `::-webkit-scrollbar` rule and draw native, wide scrollbars with a track: never set them globally; reserve them for Firefox inside `@supports not selector(::-webkit-scrollbar) { * { scrollbar-width: thin; scrollbar-color: <thumb> transparent } }`. HORIZONTAL SCROLLERS: Roam itself sets `scrollbar-color: transparent transparent` (`rgba(0,0,0,.3) transparent` on :hover) on `.rm-block__self--horizontal-scroller`, the horizontal scroller of NATIVE TABLES, so they keep native scrollbars and ignore the webkit rules: to style them, reset `scrollbar-color: auto; scrollbar-width: auto` on it and its :hover (inside `@supports selector(::-webkit-scrollbar)`, so Firefox keeps its fallback), then e.g. reveal the thumb on hover as Roam does (`.rm-block__self--horizontal-scroller::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:horizontal { background: transparent }`, `.rm-block__self--horizontal-scroller:hover::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:horizontal { background: <thumb> }`). The other horizontal scrollers use `overflow-x: scroll` (always reserve the bar, even with nothing to scroll) and follow the global webkit rules: kanban columns `.kanban-board .kanban-column-container` (0,2,0), `{{table}}` `.roam-table`, datalog tables `.rm-data-table__table`, queries in the right sidebar `#right-sidebar .rm-full-width`: switch them to `overflow-x: auto` so the bar appears only when needed.\n- Other extensions may define their own :root variables (e.g. `--cl-*` from Color Highlighter, `--icon-color-*`); Roam also loads libraries (PDF viewer, tldraw canvas, Font Awesome) whose variables are irrelevant to a theme: ignore them.";

